| `tests.workers` | integer | `4`; absent, 0, which its reader reports as `[using default] tests.workers = 0` | a whole number, 0 or more | `tests/isolation_guard.py` (`worker_count`), called by `tests/conftest.py`'s answer to pytest-xdist's `-n auto`, through `scripts/config_loader.py`'s `tests.workers` row | Sets how many pytest-xdist worker processes `make test`, and so `make verify`, runs the suite on; 0 runs it in one process. A worker that ends without handing the controller its exemption record fails the run. A negative or non-integer value stops pytest before any test runs, naming this key. | a tier target, a direct `pytest` or a nested session, which pass no `-n` and stay in one process | always |
